From f7fe4c0f75c3cb1e314c4fd6d6a3d0480facaaad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Bernhard M. Wiedemann" <bwiedemann@suse.de>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:45:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] powerpc: Restore all registers after a traced syscall again

Patch-mainline: Not yet, https://github.com/bmwiedemann/linux/commit/f7fe4c0f75c3cb1e314c4fd6d6a3d0480facaaad
References: jsc#PED-15113 git-fixes

Since the switch to GENERIC_ENTRY, register changes a tracer makes at a
syscall stop no longer reach the tracee: on return from a 64-bit sc,
r0, r4..r12, CTR and XER come back zeroed.

syscall_exit_prepare() asks the exit assembly to reload all GPRs, CTR
and XER from pt_regs only if the thread flags contain
_TIF_SYSCALL_DOTRACE. Under GENERIC_ENTRY, ptrace, seccomp, audit and
the syscall tracepoints no longer set TIF_SYSCALL_TRACE, TIF_SECCOMP and
friends but the SYSCALL_WORK_* bits in thread_info::syscall_work (see
set_task_syscall_work()), so the check is never true any more. A traced
syscall then returns through the fast path, unless signal work
(TIF_SIGPENDING/TIF_NOTIFY_SIGNAL) is processed on the way out or the
syscall itself set TIF_RESTOREALL (sigreturn, exec).

That path reloads only r1..r3 besides CR, LR, NIP and MSR, plus r13 on
64-bit (and r14..r31 with INTERRUPT_SANITIZE_REGISTERS). 64-bit sc
zeroes r0, r4..r12, CTR and XER; 32-bit leaves kernel values in the
volatile registers and does not reload r13..r31. The scv fast path also
restores r0 and r4..r8 (LR and CTR are clobbered by rfscv), so replaying
an scv still works, but tracer changes to the other registers are lost
there too.

This breaks tracers that resume a stopped syscall differently, for
example ones that re-execute the syscall instruction by moving the NIP
back by 4 at the syscall-exit stop with the syscall number put back
into r0: the sc then runs with r0 = 0, which is __NR_restart_syscall.
dettrace fails like this with "No filter rule for system call:
restart_syscall". A tracer that writes r4 at the syscall-exit stop of an
sc sees the tracee continue with r4 = 0 instead; with a 7.1 kernel
both work.

Check the equivalent syscall_work bits instead, and drop the now unused
_TIF_SYSCALL_DOTRACE. This brings back the pre-7.2 cost for traced
tasks, including every task with a seccomp filter, which takes the full
restore on each syscall exit again. The TIF_SYSCALL_* and TIF_SECCOMP
bits themselves are unused on powerpc now as well; that is left for a
separate cleanup.

A backport also needs commit c7585b8e99ad ("powerpc: Don't drop
_TIF_RESTOREALL on syscall restart"), without which the flag can still
be lost when a Book3S-64 syscall exit is restarted (pending soft-masked
interrupt or an interrupt in the restartable exit window).

Fixes: bee25f97ad24 ("powerpc: Enable GENERIC_ENTRY feature")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org # 7.2.x: c7585b8e99ad: powerpc: Don't drop _TIF_RESTOREALL on syscall restart
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org # 7.2.x
Assisted-by: LLM
---
Testing: a small tracer (pokes r4 at the syscall-exit stop of an sc,
and replays a syscall by moving NIP back with a new r0) shows both
writes lost on a ppc64le 6.12 distribution kernel carrying the
GENERIC_ENTRY backport (openSUSE Leap 16.1, 6.12.0-160100.5) and both
working on 7.1.8. The fix itself has only been build-tested
(ppc64le_defconfig, clang, W=1); it has not been booted yet.

Not changed here, and the same before 7.2: register writes a tracer
makes at a syscall-entry stop before resuming with PTRACE_CONT, or at a
PTRACE_EVENT stop without syscall tracing or seccomp, still take the
fast path.
---
 arch/powerpc/include/asm/thread_info.h |  3 ---
 arch/powerpc/kernel/interrupt.c        | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/powerpc/include/asm/thread_info.h b/arch/powerpc/include/asm/thread_info.h
index 1e069a2e7ce8..0e8dc71c8d3f 100644
--- a/arch/powerpc/include/asm/thread_info.h
+++ b/arch/powerpc/include/asm/thread_info.h
@@ -142,9 +142,6 @@ void arch_setup_new_exec(void);
 #define _TIF_SYSCALL_TRACEPOINT	(1<<TIF_SYSCALL_TRACEPOINT)
 #define _TIF_EMULATE_STACK_STORE	(1<<TIF_EMULATE_STACK_STORE)
 #define _TIF_SYSCALL_EMU	(1<<TIF_SYSCALL_EMU)
-#define _TIF_SYSCALL_DOTRACE	(_TIF_SYSCALL_TRACE | _TIF_SYSCALL_AUDIT | \
-				 _TIF_SECCOMP | _TIF_SYSCALL_TRACEPOINT | \
-				 _TIF_SYSCALL_EMU)
 
 #define _TIF_USER_WORK_MASK	(_TIF_SIGPENDING | _TIF_NEED_RESCHED | \
 				 _TIF_NEED_RESCHED_LAZY | _TIF_NOTIFY_RESUME | \
diff --git a/arch/powerpc/kernel/interrupt.c b/arch/powerpc/kernel/interrupt.c
index 55f9c0c9922a..524c51104e4c 100644
--- a/arch/powerpc/kernel/interrupt.c
+++ b/arch/powerpc/kernel/interrupt.c
@@ -75,6 +75,18 @@ static notrace __always_inline bool prep_irq_for_enabled_exit(bool restartable)
 	return true;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Syscall work after which the exit must reload all registers from
+ * pt_regs: a tracer may have changed any of them at a syscall or seccomp
+ * stop, or under PTRACE_SYSEMU. Audit and the tracepoint are included to
+ * keep the pre-GENERIC_ENTRY behaviour.
+ */
+#define PPC_SYSCALL_WORK_RESTOREALL	(SYSCALL_WORK_SECCOMP |		\
+					 SYSCALL_WORK_SYSCALL_TRACEPOINT | \
+					 SYSCALL_WORK_SYSCALL_TRACE |	\
+					 SYSCALL_WORK_SYSCALL_EMU |	\
+					 SYSCALL_WORK_SYSCALL_AUDIT)
+
 /*
  * This should be called after a syscall returns, with r3 the return value
  * from the syscall. If this function returns non-zero, the system call
@@ -117,9 +129,9 @@ notrace unsigned long syscall_exit_prepare(unsigned long r3,
 		regs->gpr[3] = r3;
 	}
 
-	if (unlikely(ti_flags & _TIF_SYSCALL_DOTRACE)) {
+	if (unlikely(READ_ONCE(current_thread_info()->syscall_work) &
+		     PPC_SYSCALL_WORK_RESTOREALL))
 		ret |= _TIF_RESTOREALL;
-	}
 
 	syscall_exit_to_user_mode(regs);
 
-- 
